# ─── Forward-looking scaffold ────────────────────────────────
# IMPORTANT: no code in netlify/functions/ currently reads any of the keys in
# the sections BELOW this one. They exist to establish the env convention ahead
# of the planned additions (CORS tightening, upstream proxy fallback, per-call
# timeout tuning). When a function is updated to consume one of these, default
# the value to the current hardcoded behavior so missing env doesn't break a run.
#
# Copy this file to .env (gitignored) and fill in real values.

# ─── Weekly refresh ──────────────────────────────────────────
# No keys here any more, and no secret. The refresh was a Worker cron that read
# its settings from wrangler.toml [vars] and committed through the GitHub API
# with GH_TOKEN, a personal access token with write access to this repository.
#
# It is .github/workflows/refresh-data.yml now: a runner with this repository
# checked out, so the plan (netlify/functions/refresh-data.js, driven by
# scripts/refresh-static.js) reads its baselines from the working tree, writes
# what changed, and commits with the workflow's own token. Nothing to configure,
# and no long-lived credential to lose.

# ─── Routing / CORS ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional: lock down Access-Control-Allow-Origin for fetch-data / fetch-crude.
# Leave unset to keep the current "*" (open) behavior.
# ALLOWED_ORIGIN=https://your-dashboard.example.com

# ─── Optional upstream proxies ────────────────────────────────
# If RBI / Yahoo / PPAC start blocking direct calls from the function region,
# point at a proxy you control. Leave unset to hit hosts directly.
# RBI_BASE_URL=https://www.rbi.org.in
# YAHOO_BASE_URL=https://query1.finance.yahoo.com
# PPAC_BASE_URL=https://ppac.gov.in

# ─── Sync write path ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional: makes every write to /data-sync require this token as the
# x-sync-token header (401 otherwise). Read by netlify/functions/data-sync.js.
#
# Worth setting on a public deploy. Without it the write path is open by design
# — the dashboard sends the token from localStorage("rbi-sync-token") when one is
# set — and while the function validates and sanitises everything it stores,
# validation stops markup but not a well-formed false record. A token is the only
# thing that keeps wrong numbers out of the shared cache.
# SYNC_WRITE_TOKEN=

# ─── Function tuning ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Per-function HTTP timeout in milliseconds — a cap on ONE upstream call, not on
# the request. Nothing cuts a Worker off at ten seconds any more, so these exist
# only so a single slow upstream cannot eat the whole request's time.
# HTTP_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_MS=10000
# YAHOO_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_MS=6000
